    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 29-layer planar dielectric stack with incident medium air and substrate fused silica. Layer sequence is fixed as alternating Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) starting and ending with Ta2O5 (Gao), with layer 15 (the middle layer, SiO2 (Lemarchand)) serving as the defect cavity. Optimize all 29 layer thicknesses with bounds 50-400 nm. Initialize mirror layers (1-14 and 16-29) at quarter-wave optical thickness for 1550 nm and the cavity layer (15) at half-wave optical thickness for 1550 nm. Objective: maximize mean transmittance at 1550 nm (single wavelength), minimize mean transmittance in 1400-1500 nm band, minimize mean transmittance in 1600-1700 nm band. Use coherent smatrix solver at normal incidence. Materials Ta2O5 (Gao) and SiO2 (Lemarchand) resolved from registry.",
    "normalized_request_english": "Optimize thicknesses of a 29-layer planar stack (Air | 29 finite layers | Fused Silica) consisting of alternating Ta2O5 and SiO2, starting and ending with Ta2O5, with layer 15 forced as SiO2. All layers bounded to 50–400 nm. Initialize Ta layers at ~180 nm and Si layers at ~270 nm for 1550 nm illumination. Use coherent smatrix TMM at normal incidence. Maximize mean transmittance at 1550 nm, minimize mean transmittance in 1400–1500 nm, and minimize mean transmittance in 1600–1700 nm.",
